OL,3,GNEWSATree flinging contest a
OL,4,A"much-loved" festive event
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt is not until the New Year that
OL,7,Fpeople traditionally throw away their
OL,8,FChristmas trees.
OL,10,FBut one event near Battle, in East
OL,11,FSussex, is trying to change all that by
OL,12,Fseeing who can fling a festive spruce
OL,13,Fthe furthest before December even
OL,14,Fstarts.
OL,16,FHeld on Saturday, the contest at
OL,17,FCatsfield Christmas Tree Farm has
OL,18,Fbecome something of an official winter
OL,19,Fsport in the area since it originated
OL,20,Fin 2020, attracting competitors from
OL,21,Fall across the South East.
OL,23,APub: 08-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,330,320,200,140,0,100
